+/// The row a replay of `job` writes, or the refusal that says this job has no second life.
+///
+/// The value is the whole row rather than a list of columns to set, and that is deliberate: it is
+/// what lets the in-memory backend assign it and the durable one write the fields it holds, so
+/// that neither of them can decide anything this function did not.
+///
